## Appendix A — Methodology

SamaritanX (operator: `{{ operator }}`) ran an agentic pipeline against the target:

1. **Recon Agent** — passive sources (crt.sh, certspotter, hackertarget) plus subfinder / amass when present, DNS brute force, and live HTTP probing with tech fingerprinting.
2. **Crawler Agent** — depth-bounded HTML walk, headless JS render, GraphQL introspection probe, secret regex sweep.
3. **Vulnerability Agent** — fan-out to {{ scanner_count }} scanners (SQLi, XSS, SSRF, IDOR, CSRF, upload, open-redirect, CORS, cache poisoning, RCE/SSTI, API top-10, prompt injection) plus an optional nuclei sweep.
4. **Logic Agent** — sensitive path enumeration, anonymous admin checks, pricing tampering, race-condition probes.
5. **Exploit Agent** — per-finding playbook + chain detection.
6. **Reporting Agent** — this document.

Stealth: rate-limited at {{ rate_limit }} req/s globally, per-host capped, jittered, randomized user-agents{% if proxy %} via `{{ proxy }}`{% endif %}.

